#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# min_max

#% text
# `min_max(xs)` gives `[min(xs), max(xs)]`; `min_max(xs, d)` widens the interval by `d` on each side, `min_max(xs, [d1, d2])` by `d1` below and `d2` above.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# An association stands for its values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
min_max([3, 1, 4, 1, 5])
#% output
#= [1, 5]

#% cell
min_max([3, 1, 4], 1)
#% output
#= [0, 5]

#% cell
min_max([3, 1, 4], [1, 2])
#% output
#= [0, 6]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
min_max([pi, e, 3])
#% output
#= [e, pi]

#% cell
min_max(assoc(a -> 2, b -> 7))
#% output
#= [2, 7]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `min`, `max`, `interval`
